This package bundles no third-party package. Three small pieces of src/node/docx.ts are adapted
from other projects, so that the DOCX reader's size checks read a file exactly as mammoth will;
their notices are reproduced at the end of this file:

  The zip directory walk (end-of-central-directory and central-directory reading, and path
  resolution), adapted from JSZip 3.10, used under the MIT License.
  The XML entity decoding, adapted from @xmldom/xmldom 0.8, MIT License.
  The relationship path joining, adapted from mammoth 1.x, BSD 2-Clause License.

It depends on the following packages, which are installed alongside it under their own licences:

Runtime dependencies
  zod                 MIT           https://github.com/colinhacks/zod
  libphonenumber-js   MIT           https://gitlab.com/catamphetamine/libphonenumber-js
                      Its phone number metadata is derived from Google's libphonenumber
                      (Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/google/libphonenumber).

Optional peer dependencies (only for reading files with /node)
  pdfjs-dist          Apache-2.0    https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js
  pdf-parse           Apache-2.0    https://github.com/mehmet-kozan/pdf-parse
  mammoth             BSD-2-Clause  https://github.com/mwilliamson/mammoth.js

Education levels follow the International Standard Classification of Education (ISCED 2011),
published by UNESCO. The level numbers are referenced, not reproduced. Spoken-language levels
follow the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (CEFR), published by the Council
of Europe; the level names A1 to C2 are referenced, not reproduced.

